# This repo is a monorepo: the Next.js dashboard (deployed here on Vercel)
# lives alongside the Python Discord bot + API backend (deployed
# separately on Railway, as one long-running process via api_server.py).
#
# Without this file, Vercel's zero-config detection treats every file in
# api/*.py as its own Python serverless function and rebuilds the entire
# backend dependency stack (discord.py, aiohttp, asyncpg, etc, ~340MB)
# once per file — slow, wasteful, and pointless since none of it is
# actually served from Vercel; api_server.py already serves these same
# handlers as plain functions from one persistent Railway process.
api/
*.py
requirements.txt
pyproject.toml
uv.lock
.python-version
discord_bot/
sql/

# unlock-pages/ is its own separate Next.js app deployed to GitHub Pages,
# not part of this Vercel project.
unlock-pages/

# Misc backend-only assets not needed for the frontend build.
*.ttf
*.sql
